{{also|Gravitation}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷreh₂-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|gravitātiō}}. Equivalent to {{af|en|gravity|-ation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɡɹævɪˈteɪʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-gravitation.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|physics}} The [[fundamental force]] of [[attraction]] that exists between all [[particle]]s with [[mass]] in the [[universe]]. It is the [[weakest]] of the four forces, and possesses a [[gauge boson]] known as the [[graviton]].

====Antonyms====
*[[levitation]]

